Complaints can be made by letter, telephone, email or in person, and may be raised with anyone in the firm. The Client Resolution team can be reached:
- by email at complaints@fernhillwealth.example;
- by telephone on 0117 496 0355, 09:00 to 17:30 on working days;
- by post to Client Resolution, Fernhill Wealth, Fernhill House, 22 Harbourside Walk, Bristol, BS1 5XY.

There is no charge for making a complaint, and making one will not affect the service you receive. If someone is complaining on your behalf, we need your written permission before we can discuss your affairs with them.

If we can resolve your complaint to your satisfaction within three working days, we confirm this in a summary resolution letter, which also explains your right to go to the Financial Ombudsman Service. Otherwise we acknowledge your complaint in writing within five working days and tell you who is handling it. More details are on the complaints page: https://www.fernhillwealth.example/complaints/

I'm sorry for your loss. I've passed your details to a qualified adviser, who will contact you. You can also call the switchboard on 0117 496 0100.

We will need:
- the original or a certified copy of the death certificate;
- details of the executors or administrators of the estate;
- the grant of probate or letters of administration (in Scotland, Confirmation) before assets can be released. If the total held with us is below £30,000, we can usually release assets to the personal representatives without a grant, against a signed indemnity.

When we are notified, any discretionary mandate ends. The portfolio is held as it is until the personal representatives instruct us. Our management and custody fees stop from the date of death. We provide a date-of-death valuation for the estate free of charge.
